WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.210
The 1970s and 1980s.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.150
Britain's coal-fired power
stations release sulfur dioxide.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.390
It combines with water
vapour to form acid rain,

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.690
which can travel long distances.

5
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.930
In Scandinavia, it falls
on forests and lakes,

6
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.010
badly damaging habitats.

7
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.990
It was the big energy worry of its day.

8
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.250
So why do we hear so
little about acid rain now?

9
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.810
Did it move elsewhere?

10
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.870
Did scientists get it wrong?

11
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.990
In this mission, you'll compare energy
efficiency with reducing demand,

12
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.090
and test the UK's strategies
to cut energy use.

13
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.630
Then you'll weigh three
energy issues: acid rain,

14
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.190
the enhanced greenhouse
effect, and nuclear waste.

15
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.730
Your mission: explain why we hear
so little about acid rain today.
